## Acceptance

By using the software, you agree to all of the terms and conditions below.

## Free Use

You may use, copy, and modify the software free of charge, and run your modified copies, for any of
the following:

1. personal use by an individual, including personal side projects that earn money;
2. education, meaning teaching, studying, or academic research at an accredited school or university;
3. work on an open-source project, meaning a project whose source code is distributed under a
   license approved by the Open Source Initiative, when that work is not paid for by a company that
   is not a Small Company;
4. use by a non-profit organization; and
5. any use by or on behalf of a Small Company.

## Commercial Use

Any use of the software by or on behalf of a company that is not a Small Company, other than the
uses in items 1 to 4 of Free Use, requires an active paid subscription to the Ferryx Team plan or a
higher plan, covering each person in that company who uses the software. "Use on behalf of a
company" includes use by its employees and contractors for its work.

## Transition Period

Until the Ferryx Team plan is available for purchase, and for 90 days after the date it first
becomes available, a company that is not a Small Company may use the software for its work free of
charge. After that period, Commercial Use applies.

## Self-Hosted Relay

Anyone, including a company that is not a Small Company, may run the Ferryx relay server
(`ferryx-relay`) on their own infrastructure free of charge. This does not remove the subscription
requirement in Commercial Use for the desktop application, the command-line tools, or the mobile and
web clients.

